{
  "id": "kth-smallest-element-in-a-sorted-matrix",
  "questionId": "kth-smallest-element-in-a-sorted-matrix",
  "slug": "kth-smallest-element-in-a-sorted-matrix",
  "title": "Kth Smallest Element in a Sorted Matrix",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Heap",
  "patterns": [
    "heap",
    "matrix",
    "min-heap",
    "top k"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "the matrix's row-sorted and column-sorted structure means you never need to look at every element",
    "the smallest unseen value is always at the front of some row - which row's front is smallest changes as you consume elements",
    "seed a min-heap with the first element of every row, tagged with its row and column",
    "pop the smallest k times; each time you pop an element, push the next element in that same row (if one exists). the kth pop is your answer"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "flattening and sorting the whole matrix when k is small, doing far more work than needed",
    "seeding the heap with the first row instead of the first column (or vice versa) and getting the row/column advance direction backwards",
    "forgetting to guard against pushing past the last column of a row, causing an out-of-bounds access"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a square matrix where every row is sorted in ascending\norder left to right, and every column is sorted in ascending order top\nto bottom, along with an integer `k`.\n\n**Find the `k`th smallest value in the entire matrix.**\n\nDuplicates count separately, so if the value 5 appears three times, it\ncan occupy three consecutive ranks.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "matrix is n x n",
      "1 <= k <= n*n",
      "each row and each column is individually sorted ascending"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "1x1 matrix",
      "k = 1 (the minimum value)",
      "k = n*n (the maximum value)",
      "duplicate values across rows and columns"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "matrix = [[1, 5, 9], [10, 11, 13], [12, 13, 15]], k = 8",
        "output": "13",
        "expectedOutput": "13",
        "explanation": "all nine values sorted are 1,5,9,10,11,12,13,13,15; the 8th value is 13"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
